WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:07.200
This now brings us to the end of this advanced landscape tutorial series.

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.199
I'd just like to quickly recap what we went over when we first started with our initial project setup,

3
00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:16.199
and that was setting up a new project based off of the third person template.

4
00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:24.199
We then enabled some plugins, edited our INI files, imported some textures and some static meshes,

5
00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:28.199
and then we moved on to creating our landscape material.

6
00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:36.200
Now remember, our landscape material allowed us to have the various textures displayed based off the slope of the landscape

7
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.200
instead of having to go in and define them or paint them manually by hand.

8
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:48.420
We then took a look at how we could utilize displacement inside of our landscape materials

9
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.420
to give our landscape materials a more defined and realistic look.

10
00:00:53.420 --> 00:01:00.420
We also looked at how we can adjust our material for our landscape so that in the distance,

11
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.420
the tiling artifacts are not as apparent as they would be.

12
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:11.420
We then looked at how we could implement landscape grass and some interesting ways to control its placement on the landscape.

13
00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:17.420
We also took a look at how we can utilize landscape physical materials that will allow us to define

14
00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:23.420
different physical properties of different surfaces that are used within our landscape.

15
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:30.420
Next, we looked at how we could edit our level using things such as gizmo brushes

16
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:37.420
and even utilizing hand painted brushes, as well as how to utilize level instanced actors,

17
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:46.420
level packed actors, landscape patches, and finally finishing with how to utilize and adjust HLODs on our landscape.

18
00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:53.420
I hope you enjoyed this video tutorial series as much as I enjoyed having you, and I will see you next time.
